pi5-stm32-slam

The stm32_base_bridge package is derived from:
https://github.com/datttzz/linoafterfix (Apache-2.0).
Its original package metadata and source attribution are retained.
Changes in this project: IMU topic routing, CAN feedback freshness checks,
explicit motor-enable policy, input validation and configurable startup logs.

Hardware dimensions are initial values from the RPBot profile in linoafterfix.
Confirm sensor mounting and dimensions on the final vehicle.

STM32 firmware is maintained separately:
https://github.com/nguyenbinh-shark/Microros_H723_USB
This repository does not distribute or reflash that firmware.

External dependencies retain their upstream licenses. The micro-ROS agent
builder downloads upstream sources into an ignored local workspace.

Nino Real Test integration:
The training feature formulas and kinematics helpers are extracted from the
user-supplied Ninobot_controlled_with_torque-add_rl_2-main (1).zip.
Source repository: https://github.com/datttzz/Ninobot_controlled_with_torque-add_rl_2
The nino_control package metadata declares Apache-2.0. Original files and
upstream notices are retained where supplied. Source hashes are recorded in
SOURCE_PROVENANCE.json. This distribution contains no model weights.

New real-robot adapter: explicit hardware contract, feedback-clocked PI,
deterministic CPU SAC inference, safe-reference routing, arm/disarm logic,
freshness/ownership checks and local JSONL diagnostics.
